From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Youwes09 <yuvi.shen@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 23:46:27 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132: Treat the fastest CPU states as
 normal states

The P cluster's 4416 and 4464 MHz and the E cluster's 2892 MHz were
turbo states, but schedutil caps its requests at the frequency each
policy had when it was created, before boost can be enabled, so it never
asked for them. They need no boost: the cluster clamps any request to
what its busy cores allow, 3936 MHz with four P cores busy. With one
busy P core and 4464 MHz requested, a J713 averages 4168 MHz.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Youwes09 <yuvi.shen@outlook.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi | 3 ---
 1 file changed, 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi
index 5420c354edb7..156f8796f888 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi
@@ -278,7 +278,6 @@ opp08 {
 			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <2892000000>;
 			opp-level = <8>;
 			opp-microwatt = <582776>;
-			turbo-mode;
 		};
 	};
 
@@ -398,14 +397,12 @@ opp19 {
 			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <4416000000>;
 			opp-level = <19>;
 			opp-microwatt = <5776890>;
-			turbo-mode;
 		};
 
 		opp20 {
 			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <4464000000>;
 			opp-level = <20>;
 			opp-microwatt = <5940083>;
-			turbo-mode;
 		};
 	};
 
